  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As we observe from left to right in a period, there is a gradual increase in ionization potential due to the increase in Nuclear charge.<br />From left to right, the elements will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>Ti</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>22</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>Mn</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>25</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>Ni</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>Zn</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>)</mo></math> .<br />Hence, the correct order will be:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ti</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Ni</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
